{
 "about": "Monte Carlo cross-check of the exact engine against an independent coalescent simulator (msprime; Baumdicker et al. 2022, Genetics 220: iyab229): per battery, one non-recombining genealogy per replicate (sim_ancestry with ploidy 1, population size 1, the stated model and seed), L_i = total branch length subtending i samples, sample means of L_i ('first'), L_i L_j ('second', full matrix) and the normalized q_ij = mean(L_i L_j)/mean(L_tot^2) ('q'), with bootstrap standard deviations (300 resamples). Kingman batteries are compared raw (time units agree) and normalized; Beta (simulator alpha = 1.5, here alpha = 3/2) and the simulator's Dirac model (psi = 0.5, c = 10; lambda_exact.msprime_dirac_rate(1/2, 10)) are compared on q only (the model time scale cancels). z = (MC mean - exact)/sd, rounded to 3 decimals; worst |z| over the 72 statistics is 1.798 (acceptance rule |z| < 4). This is a float-register CHECK of the exact engine, not part of any certificate. The package battery recomputes every z from these stored means/sds and the live exact values.",
